WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
A flower receives pollen.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.800
Is that already a new plant?

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.960
Not yet.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.200
The egg is in a different place inside

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.119
the flower.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.080
Let's follow a successful flowering-plant example, from pollen

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.280
arriving to an embryo inside a seed.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.440
The embryo is the young plant that can

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.120
later grow from that seed.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.413
First, find the egg.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.813
The flower has a swollen part called the

00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:25.693
ovary.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.853
Inside it are structures called ovules.

00:00:29.134 --> 00:00:31.773
In our selected ovule, an egg cell lies

00:00:32.054 --> 00:00:32.653
inside.

00:00:32.974 --> 00:00:35.613
Sperm and egg are reproductive cells that can

00:00:36.054 --> 00:00:36.533
join.

00:00:36.574 --> 00:00:38.813
The sperm must reach this egg before the

00:00:38.894 --> 00:00:40.733
young plant can begin in the route we

00:00:40.814 --> 00:00:41.533
are following.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.453
Pollen is produced in the flower's anthers.

00:00:45.694 --> 00:00:48.093
When pollen reaches a receiving surface called the

00:00:48.174 --> 00:00:50.773
stigma, that is pollination.

00:00:51.054 --> 00:00:53.053
The stigma is above the ovary in this

00:00:53.134 --> 00:00:53.693
model.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.013
The pollen is on the stigma, while the

00:00:56.174 --> 00:00:58.573
egg is still down inside an ovule.

00:00:58.814 --> 00:01:01.453
Pollen arriving does not mean sperm and egg

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:02.333
have joined.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:06.653
When compatible pollen lands on a suitable stigma,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.733
it can grow a pollen tube.

00:01:08.814 --> 00:01:11.133
The tube grows down through the flower towards

00:01:11.214 --> 00:01:12.333
an ovule.

00:01:12.414 --> 00:01:15.693
Sperm cells associated with that pollen travel inside

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:16.813
the tube.

00:01:16.894 --> 00:01:19.293
The tube reaches the ovule and delivers sperm

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:20.653
near the egg.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.213
So the tube bridges the distance between pollen

00:01:23.294 --> 00:01:25.693
arriving at the top and the egg waiting

00:01:25.894 --> 00:01:26.813
inside the ovule.

00:01:28.034 --> 00:01:30.233
One sperm cell joins the egg.

00:01:30.514 --> 00:01:32.353
That event is fertilisation.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:35.473
The fertilised egg can divide and develop into

00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:37.633
an embryo, a young plant.

00:01:37.874 --> 00:01:40.273
We are following the embryo-forming part of this

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:41.953
flower's reproductive route.

00:01:42.194 --> 00:01:45.393
This is sexual reproduction because sperm and egg

00:01:45.474 --> 00:01:46.353
joined.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:49.073
The pollen was the arrival stage; joining at

00:01:49.154 --> 00:01:51.633
the egg starts the embryo's development.

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:56.113
As development continues, the ovule develops into a

00:01:56.314 --> 00:01:58.353
seed containing the embryo.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.993
The embryo is the young plant inside; it

00:02:01.114 --> 00:02:02.913
is not the whole seed.

00:02:02.954 --> 00:02:06.353
The seed's outer covering protects what is inside.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:10.113
Later, if conditions support germination, the embryo can

00:02:10.274 --> 00:02:12.593
begin growing out into a seedling.

00:02:12.754 --> 00:02:14.993
Making the seed and growing the seedling are

00:02:15.154 --> 00:02:16.193
different stages.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.200
Try this changed case.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.880
Compatible pollen reaches the stigma.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.160
Its pollen tube starts growing but stops before

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.640
reaching the only ovule in this model.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.520
No other pollen tube reaches that ovule.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.200
Has pollination happened?

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.480
Has this egg been fertilised?

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.800
Explain whether the embryo-forming route we followed can

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:38.720
continue.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.560
Pause and use the locations in the picture.

00:02:56.967 --> 00:03:00.006
Pollination happened because pollen reached the stigma.

00:03:00.487 --> 00:03:03.366
But this tube stopped before reaching the ovule,

00:03:03.447 --> 00:03:04.966
and no other tube reached it.

00:03:05.527 --> 00:03:07.846
The sperm was not delivered to this egg,

00:03:07.927 --> 00:03:10.166
so the egg was not fertilised.

00:03:10.487 --> 00:03:13.766
The embryo-forming pathway we followed cannot continue from

00:03:13.887 --> 00:03:14.646
this egg.

00:03:14.967 --> 00:03:18.006
This is why pollen arriving and fertilisation are

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.126
different events: the sperm still needs a route

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:21.846
to the egg.

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:26.266
Keep the two landmarks in mind: pollen arrives

00:03:26.307 --> 00:03:29.386
at the stigma; sperm joins the egg inside

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:30.106
the ovule.

00:03:30.587 --> 00:03:32.826
Arrival is not joining.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:35.546
That short contrast helps you explain a stopped

00:03:35.627 --> 00:03:38.746
tube rather than just remember two definitions.

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:41.946
After joining, the fertilised egg develops into an

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.746
embryo while the ovule becomes a seed around

00:03:44.827 --> 00:03:44.986
it.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.626
Next, we will follow a strawberry stem that

00:03:47.707 --> 00:03:49.866
makes another plant without a seed.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.626
If you would like notes, copy these now,

00:03:53.707 --> 00:03:55.226
or pause for longer.
